      "run": 1,
      "steps": 4,
      "narrative": "Upon entering the cramped galley, I was immediately struck by the pervasive scent of salt and the sight of a dented metal kettle lying on the floor, its presence a testament to the hard life aboard. Taking the kettle into my hands, I felt the roughness of tin, a material that had seen better days. The space was functional, almost to the point of austere, with its singular focus on the preparation of food amidst a backdrop of maritime rigors.\n\nDeciding to explore further, I navigated through a narrow doorway to a storeroom, finding it oddly dormant yet heavy with the air of past activity; the scent of paraffin clung to the sparse shelves. Here, amidst the dust and the faint echo of footsteps long past, I located a coil of rope\u2014perhaps intended for securing cargo or repairs\u2014and felt its rough texture slide under my fingers as I added it to my collection.\n\nContinuing my journey upward via a stair to the east, I left behind the remnants of the galley and storeroom's stories, each object a frozen moment in the passage",
